					</div><!-- /comment-identifier -->

					<div class="comment-content">
						<div class="bpgsites_comment_posted_in">
<p>Posted in: <a href="https://commons.digitalthoreau.org/groups/panel-of-experts/">Panel of Experts</a></p>
</div>
<p>The drawing of T&#8217;s cabin was made by his sister Sophia, an amateur artist. T himself complained of it, &#8220;Thoreau would suggest a little alteration, chiefly in the door, in the wide projection of the roof at the front; and that the bank more immediately about the house be brought out more distinctly&#8221; (Sanborn, 1917, 338). Sanborn adds, &#8220;He must have noticed that her trees were firs and pines, with a few deciduous tress that did not then grow there.&#8221; Ellery Channing thought it a &#8220;feeble caricature.&#8221; Other contemporary drawings of the cabin may be found in Meltzer and Harding (144-5).</p>

					</div><!-- /comment-content -->

